{
  "rationale": "The plant models the robot's sensor and motion interface, separating perception and actuation. The specification encodes a safe, coverage-biased exploration policy: random_walk is used in clear/search states, move_forward is used for short progress, and obstacle events trigger conservative, one-shot turn or scan actions. Recovery states only allow safe turns or, as a last resort, a full scan. The supervisor always returns to exploration as soon as the path is clear, and never enables forward/coverage actions in obstacle states.",
  "strategy": [
    "Separate plant for perception and actuation; specification binds sensor outcomes to safe actions.",
    "Bias toward random_walk and short forward moves in clear states; use single-action recovery states for obstacles; never allow move_forward or random_walk in obstacle states; always return to exploration after recovery."
  ],
